title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 24

= Inter-Party Relationships

Our coalition does not exist in isolation. There are other political forces in the country - some worth trying to work with, others worth trying to peel apart.

- @gop_establishment: Reach out to the traditional, establishment wing of the Republican Party.
- @greens: Build relations with the Green Party.
- @libertarians: Build relations with the Libertarian Party.
- @stand_alone: Focus entirely on our own coalition for now.
- @easy_discard

@gop_establishment
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1;
go-to: gop_estab_trump_dominant if trump_dominance >= 60; gop_estab_contested if trump_dominance >= 30 and trump_dominance < 60; gop_estab_open if trump_dominance < 30

@gop_estab_trump_dominant
on-arrival: gop_estab_relation += 3*(1-dissent); maga_share += 0.3; gop_estab_share -= 0.3;

Trump's personal grip on the party is near-total. Establishment-wing Republicans who might otherwise be open to working with us are wary of being seen as disloyal, and few are willing to be publicly associated with us. Still, quiet channels remain open.

[? if gop_estab_relation >= 55 : Some of these establishment figures privately welcome our overtures, even if they can't say so on the record. ?]

@gop_estab_contested
on-arrival: gop_estab_relation += 6*(1-dissent); maga_share -= 0.5; gop_estab_share += 0.5;

The party's establishment wing is locked in a real internal fight over its own direction. Our outreach - focused on shared institutional concerns rather than ideology - gives wavering establishment figures a reason to draw a sharper line against the party's Trumpist wing.

[? if gop_estab_relation >= 55 : These relationships are paying real dividends: several establishment-aligned members have begun distancing themselves from Trump more openly. ?]

@gop_estab_open
on-arrival: gop_estab_relation += 8*(1-dissent); maga_share -= 0.8; gop_estab_share += 0.8; establishment_dem_dissent -= 2;

With the party's establishment wing back in a position of real strength, there is a genuine opening for cross-partisan cooperation on institutional questions - defending the courts, election administration, and other guardrails - even as we remain adversaries on nearly everything else.

[? if gop_estab_relation >= 65 : This cooperation has become durable enough that some in our own coalition are starting to ask what we're getting out of it. ?]

@greens
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; green_relation += 6*(1-dissent);
go-to: greens_spoiler if working_class_green + college_educated_green >= 6; greens_marginal if working_class_green + college_educated_green < 6

@greens_spoiler
on-arrival: dirty_break_support += 1 if green_relation >= 50;

The Green Party draws real votes from our left flank in close races, and building relations with them is as much about damage control and coordination as it is about genuine alliance. Some in our insurgent wing wonder aloud whether they should simply be running as Greens instead.

@greens_marginal

Relations with the Green Party remain cordial but low-stakes for now - they poll too marginally to be a serious electoral factor either way.

@libertarians
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; libertarian_relation += 6*(1-dissent); maga_share -= 0.2 if libertarian_relation >= 45;

The Libertarian Party draws mostly from disaffected Republicans uncomfortable with Trumpism's authoritarian drift, and there is occasional common ground on civil liberties and criminal justice reform, even as we disagree on almost everything about political economy.

[? if libertarian_relation >= 45 : A meaningful bloc of libertarian-leaning voters are now genuinely up for grabs, uncomfortable with where the GOP has gone. ?]

@stand_alone

We focus entirely on building our own coalition for now, rather than reaching outward.

- @return: Continue...
